Licensing
=========

This project uses two licenses, split by what the code does.

Zen components — Apache-2.0 only
--------------------------------

The NTFS/indexing/terminal layer that came from the zen project is licensed
under the Apache License 2.0 only:

    bins/zen-rs/                        the zen CLI (NTFS indexer)
    bins/search-ui/                     the terminal UI
    crates/discovery-windows/           MFT + USN discovery (ntfs, volume, indexer, seam)
    crates/name-core/src/index.rs       the ERI2 on-disk index and its query layer

Every source file in those trees carries `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`,
and the three crate manifests state `license = "Apache-2.0"`.
This portion is not available under the MIT license. Apache-2.0 was chosen
for it because it carries an express patent grant and an explicit limitation
of liability, which a distinctive, independently valuable subsystem should
have.

Tesla Valve pack store — Apache-2.0 only
----------------------------------------

The pack-store subsystem is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 only
(inherited from rgx, which marks it the same way):

    crates/rgx-core/src/tv/             the format, the query vocabulary, the planner
    crates/rgx-core/src/tv_runtime/     the builder, searcher, store and inspector
    crates/rgx-core/src/bin/rgx-tv.rs   the rgx-tv CLI

Every file in those directories carries `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`.
This portion is not available under the MIT license.

Everything else — MIT OR Apache-2.0
-----------------------------------

All remaining code in this repository is dual-licensed under the MIT License
and the Apache License 2.0. You may use that code under the terms of either
license. Commercial use of it is licensed under Apache-2.0, which is the
license this project intends for commercial deployment; the MIT option remains
available to anyone who prefers its terms.

Full texts: LICENSE-APACHE and LICENSE-MIT. Third-party notices: NOTICE.

Consequence for the distributed binaries
----------------------------------------

`zen-rs` and `search-ui` are Apache-2.0-only code end to end, so
distributing either binary is governed by Apache-2.0. `searchd` links the
Tesla Valve pack store by default (`--tv-dir`), so distributing it likewise
distributes Apache-2.0 code and Apache-2.0 governs that distribution. The
same applies to any binary that includes `discovery-windows` or
`name_core::index`. A binary built from only the dual-licensed remainder
(for example `searchctl` without the TV store) is available under MIT or
Apache-2.0 as above.
